{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/734318-differences-between-1e-and-2e-corebooks","id":734318,"title":"Differences between 1e and 2e corebooks","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-10-28T04:41:05-07:00","id":734318,"title":"Differences between 1e and 2e corebooks","content":"Could someone please explain the differences in tone, metaplot and game premise of the 1e corebook vs the 2e corebook?<br /> Not really interested in mechanical differences and i won't be buying any supplements so please just the two corebooks.<br /> Thanks!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2671,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2671-legopaidi","user":"legopaidi","date":". 10-28-2015, 08:07 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2671-legopaidi","name":"legopaidi","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"43"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-28T04:47:50-07:00","id":734341,"title":"","content":"Is there a particular reason you are not interested in Revised or W20? The corebooks all have comparatively little metaplot difference as the corebooks don't deal with metaplot. The tone between the games is different, though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8760-cogliostro","name":"Cogliostro","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8760_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-28T05:06:33-07:00","id":734366,"title":"","content":"Yes, W20 is too expensive for me at the moment and there is a possibility of acquiring only either the 1e or the 2e corebook through a trade (and that's why Revised is out)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2671-legopaidi","name":"legopaidi","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"43"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-28T05:14:54-07:00","id":734402,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>legopaidi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/734318-differences-between-1e-and-2e-corebooks?p=734366#post734366\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, W20 is too expensive for me at the moment and there is a possibility of acquiring only either the 1e or the 2e corebook through a trade (and that's why Revised is out)</div> </div> </div> </div>In that case take 2e. It's a hardcover compared to first edition's softcover, the art is better, there are more gifts. It uses the renown system that is used in 2e/Revised/W20. It has an awesome color comic book by DiTerlizzi that literally explains everything for the Werewolf newbie. Most of the gifts and rites are 100% compatible with Revised/W20. There is more monsters and spirits in the book and the setting is much closer to what you will find in Revised and W20.<br /> <br /> If you can trade for 2e, take it! It's an excellent book, and it's pretty workable with the more modern Werewolf material.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8760-cogliostro","name":"Cogliostro","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8760_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-28T05:26:31-07:00","id":734422,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cogliostro</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/734318-differences-between-1e-and-2e-corebooks?p=734402#post734402\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> In that case take 2e. It's a hardcover compared to first edition's softcover, the art is better, there are more gifts. It uses the renown system that is used in 2e/Revised/W20. It has an awesome color comic book by DiTerlizzi that literally explains everything for the Werewolf newbie. Most of the gifts and rites are 100% compatible with Revised/W20. There is more monsters and spirits in the book and the setting is much closer to what you will find in Revised and W20.<br /> <br /> If you can trade for 2e, take it! It's an excellent book, and it's pretty workable with the more modern Werewolf material.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, but what is the actual difference in tone, premise etc?<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2671-legopaidi","name":"legopaidi","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"43"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-28T05:41:49-07:00","id":734429,"title":"","content":"Did you ever see a first edition White Wolf book? They all insist on the Punk Punk, and they are very shallow in their representation of the setting. Everything is dark and gloomy just to be dark and gloomy. This can lead to very unfortunate excesses in comic book 90isms in the first round of games White Wolf made. For Werewolf the core premise is the same, but the Wyrm becomes less Captain Planet villiany and more insidious corruption that makes your skin crawl. The Garou go from downright cardboard (and occasionally offensive) cultural stereotypes to actually being their own cultures and philosophies. The spirits get more depth and the realms are more detailed in the core.The game goes more into the responsibility rather then simplistic conclusions that Werewolves are the only good guys and that what ever they do is fine.<br /> <br /> All in all it's the same game, just done better. More thought was put into it, more context and more ideas.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8760-cogliostro","name":"Cogliostro","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8760_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-28T06:47:46-07:00","id":734572,"title":"","content":"Thank you mate! That's the info i was looking for! There's a similar thread about Vampire <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/734288-differences-between-1e-and-2e\">here</a>, would love to read your insight on it too","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2671-legopaidi","name":"legopaidi","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"43"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-28T06:55:59-07:00","id":734601,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>legopaidi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/734318-differences-between-1e-and-2e-corebooks?p=734572#post734572\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thank you mate! That's the info i was looking for! There's a similar thread about Vampire <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/734288-differences-between-1e-and-2e\">here</a>, would love to read your insight on it too</div> </div> </div> </div>I have seen only First ed Mage and Werewolf, so I cannot really say for Vampire. The first edition of Vampire I've had in my hands was Revised, but you should consider that 2nd edition of Vampire literally came out a year after the first so I assume a lot of tightening on the screws happened. The consensus online is that the WW First Editions tend to be weird and unfocused, but you really need to ask on the Vampire forum to learn more.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8760-cogliostro","name":"Cogliostro","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8760_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"505"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}